# Old Mill Road, seed 29, Code's Fun Gate play (not cold: Code retuned the map and read Chat's seed 42 entry first)
# turn 1: Wren baits the brigand so the kill and the EXP are hers; the captain stays a step behind
move wren 4,7
wait wren
move captain 2,7
wait captain
end
# turn 2: Wren finishes the brigand at 2; the captain comes up beside her
attack wren brigand-1
move captain 5,6
wait captain
end
# turn 3: Wren dresses the axe wound; both stay outside radius 4 of the soldier at 9,1
move wren 6,6
item wren 2
move captain 6,4
wait captain
end
# turn 4: the captain wakes the mill from 7,2, on plain, and takes both of them; Wren stays a bow's length out of reach
move captain 7,2
wait captain
move wren 5,4
wait wren
end
# turn 5: the soldier missed and stands at 4 on the hill; the archer is behind it at 9,2 where nothing can reach it this turn, so the captain drops the soldier and Wren steps up out of the bow line
forecast captain soldier-1
attack captain soldier-1
move wren 6,3
wait wren
end
# turn 6: the archer came down to the road to shoot Wren and is now inside both swords' reach; two strikes at one tile, no counter possible
move wren 7,3
attack wren archer-1
move captain 8,2
attack captain archer-1
end
# turn 7: the bandit holds his tile and hits for 9 on the captain and 10 on Wren; the captain dresses to full before opening, Wren stays out of his reach
item captain 2
move wren 8,3
wait wren
end
# turn 8: the captain opens alone at 22; the counter and the enemy phase cost 9 each and his own counter takes the bandit to 4
move captain 9,1
attack captain mill_bandit-1
end
# turn 9: Wren closes
move wren 10,2
attack wren mill_bandit-1
